# "run loop" = the site queue

When Matt says **run loop**, **run the loop**, **go**, **keep going until the site is
done**, or **continue as new nodes get entered**, he means the site queue. Not the
growth loop, not an audit, not a plan (Matt 2026-09-09: "run loop" never flips to
another skill). Empty of eligible is not a stop: keep the scheduled wake
(Matt 2026-09-10).

**Read first:** `.cursor/skills/site-queue/SKILL.md` — the pointer skill for a non-Claude
builder, which names the canonical protocol (`.claude/skills/site-queue/SKILL.md`) and the
four mission documents. Then work. Do not re-audit the site; the backlog already exists.

## The three commands

```bash
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --json                                    # what to take, in serve order
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --claim SITE-XX,SITE-YY --owner <owner>   # the ONLY claim path
npx tsx scripts/site-queue-status.ts --touch SITE-XX,SITE-YY --owner <owner>   # hourly, while you hold
```

`--json` carries `liveWorkers`, `maxWorkers` and `staleClaims`. **If `liveWorkers` is at or
above `maxWorkers` (3), stop and say so** — every worker spends one shared account
allowance, and four at once exhausted it and killed all of them on 2026-09-08. Otherwise
claim the first two eligible items in the JSON's order on disjoint file sets. A non-zero
exit means you got nothing: read the message, do not hand-write a claim. Claude sessions
and Grok sessions coexist by this tool alone; never coordinate by hand.

Owner name: `grok-<model>-<YYYY-MM-DD>`, or `cursor-<model>-<date>`. A claim whose
heartbeat is older than three hours is released to the next worker, so heartbeat hourly or
lose the node.

## The bar

Every SITE node's accept test is the same four steps, in order (Matt 2026-09-12): (1)
catalog source installed and imported by the route's v3 primitive (`ci:catalog-install`);
(2) navy / cream / Geist / Amboqia intact (`ci:one-design-system`); (3) no regression —
`ci:runtime-gates` ends with `ci:route-content-floor`, which holds the route's
`contentFloor` (hero width and resolution, images, video, sections, words, links, JSON-LD)
on the built page; (4) only then a **separate evaluator** — a different
model from the builder — scores the page class from shots at 1440 and 375
(`scripts/take-route-shots.mjs`), three scorings in one call, median, and the score must
rise **by at least 6** (the rise floor: a smaller rise is inside the judge's measured noise,
`taste-rule-freeze.json` `riseFloorBasis`). Receipt in the route's `parity.json` per `design_system/public/TASTE.md`, shape
checked by `scripts/lib/taste-receipt.mjs`. The instrument is the judge chain, and it
starts at the **round judge**: whatever model scored the current table
(`taste-table.json` `instrument.evaluatorModel`, `claude-sonnet-5` since 2026-09-12)
grades every route this round through the **claude CLI**; a builder of that family gets
the other claude alias and the route rebaselines once. **grok-4.6** returns only at the
next full table run, through the `grok` CLI or through the Cursor CLI (`cursor-agent
--model grok-4.6`, Matt's Cursor subscription; same model, same ruler, the table's own
link first), and when both grok-4.6 links are missing or out, the claude CLI is the last
link. Every link is a subscription CLI: **no API keys, ever** (Matt 2026-09-12). Run it with
`npx tsx scripts/taste-evaluate.ts <route-key> --builder <model>` and copy the
`evaluatorModel` it prints. A Grok lane builds with **grok-4.5**, because the gate refuses
a model grading its own page. **Who builds is also a chain** (Matt 2026-09-12):
`scripts/site-queue-routine.sh` tries the `grok` CLI, then `cursor-agent`, then the
`claude` CLI (Opus, so Sonnet stays the judge), skipping a link only on 402, not
logged in, or missing; the LaunchAgent `com.ryanrealty.site-queue` fires it six times
a day. The
rubric is frozen at `v1-2026-09-12` until every class has a table row on it
(`ci:rubric-freeze`) — fix the page or the tool, never add a rule. **Finish line: every public
page class at 70 or above on that table** (Matt 2026-09-09). Before composing a
section, `node scripts/lib/taste-catalog.mjs <class>` and fetch the modules it
prints from beautifului.dev, beui.dev, rareui.com, transitions.dev, and
ui.shadcn.com. Adapt into v3. If the job has no house primitive, add one to
`components/site/v3` (OPEN set — not a second kit). Navy, cream, Geist,
Amboqia stay. Do not invent a layout from adjectives. The evaluator prompt
includes that catalog.

Then the gates (`npm run ci:gates`), the `Node: <id>` trailer on every commit touching
`app/**` or `components/site/**` (G72), ONE `npm run push` per round from the main
checkout, `deploy:verify`, a live check on ryan-realty.com, and the evidence written on
the node — done, or blocked with `blocked_until` so it reopens itself, or blocked on Matt
with the question in ONE line in `blocked_reason`.

## Never

- Never wait on Matt mid-round: take the safe path the skill allows, write what you chose
  on the node, keep going.
- Never mark a node done from a self-report; evidence is what the environment showed.
- Never leave finished work on a branch — merge and push, or write it into
  `docs/plans/CROSS_AGENT_HANDOFF.md` before you stop.
